# GMS raises Elemental Drain's rate to 5% per burn with the same cap of five, so
# a full count is 25% instead of 15%. It supersedes instead of adding: one rate,
# the better of the two, as Advanced Blessing supersedes Bless.
#
# That makes it a bossing passive, as GMS calls it: on a map the count is at the
# cap anyway, and on a boss it is however many burns the rotation keeps on that
# one enemy.
#
# It starts just above a maxed Elemental Drain's 3% and climbs to GMS's 5%, like
# every superseding skill here; Advanced Blessing starts where Bless ends for
# the same reason.
#
# It doesn't go past its max level. GMS maxes it at 1 and doesn't mark it for
# Combat Orders, so there is no higher level to reach.
name: "Fervent Drain"
description: "Increases the effect of Elemental Drain."
kind: SKILL_KIND_PASSIVE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_FIRE_POISON_ARCH_MAGE skill_order: 10 }
max_level: 10
supersedes_skill_name: "Elemental Drain"
dot_count_cap: 5
base { final_dmg_pct_per_dot: 0.032 }
per_level { final_dmg_pct_per_dot: 0.002 }
